            "The 23-page remedy filing represents the most consequential structural enforcement action undertaken by federal trustbusters since the court-ordered breakup of AT&T in 1982 and the landmark prosecution of Microsoft in the late 1990s. Assistant Attorney General Jonathan Kanter emphasized that behavioral promises alone cannot restore competitive vitality to an online search marketplace where Google commands an insurmountable 90% domestic market share. Divesting Chrome—which controls over 67% of global browser traffic—is deemed vital by regulators because it serves as the paramount funnel steering hundreds of millions of users directly into Google's proprietary search monetization machine.",
