            "Crucially, the government's proposal establishes strict behavioral and architectural firewalls surrounding Google's Android mobile operating system. While stopping short of demanding an immediate forced divestiture of Android as part of the primary structural remedy, prosecutors explicitly urged the court to retain the right to order Android's spinoff if behavioral remedies fail to eliminate self-preferencing within twenty-four months. Furthermore, the proposal requires Google to establish a technical syndicate granting competitors real-time API access to its core search index and click-and-query data, while granting digital publishers explicit technological switches to prevent their editorial content from being used to train Google's Gemini artificial intelligence models.",
